IO-43: write a dated SAVE HOTSTART file when the run reaches its date

iface_readFileParams() stores the date and time given after a SAVE HOTSTART
file name as a DateTime (days since 12/30/1899), but hotstart_save() compared
it with NewRoutingTime, the elapsed time in milliseconds. For any date after
1900 the test passed once about 44 seconds had been simulated, and the file
held the state at that step. Compare the current date and time instead.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-43_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/hotstart.c b/src/legacy/engine/hotstart.c
index c03ca4a..0982714 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/hotstart.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/hotstart.c
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ void hotstart_save()
     {
         if (FhotstartOutputs[i].file && 
             FhotstartOutputs[i].saveDateTime > 0 && 
-            NewRoutingTime >= FhotstartOutputs[i].saveDateTime)
+            getDateTime(NewRoutingTime) >= FhotstartOutputs[i].saveDateTime)
         {
             saveRunoff(&FhotstartOutputs[i]);
             saveRouting(&FhotstartOutputs[i]);
